<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>UPDATE: Mac OS X 10.10.2 Available (Combo)</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[<DIV class=FixletMessage><TABLE><TBODY><TR><TD><P>The 10.10.2 Update is recommended for all users running Mac OS X Yosemite. It includes general operating system fixes that enhance the stability, compatibility, and security of your Mac.</P>
<P>This update is available via the IBM Endpoint Manager server, which is the default action, and Apple Software Update on the endpoint.</P>
<P>The default action does not require internet connection on the endpoints. This action downloads the installer to the IBM Endpoint Manager server and then installs the update to the endpoints.</P>
<P><STRONG>Note: </STRONG>If you want to use Apple Software Update, ensure that the endpoints have continuous internet connection to install the update successfully.</P>
<P><STRONG>Note: </STRONG>Affected computers may report back as 'Pending Restart' once the patch has run successfully, but will not report back their final status until the computer has been restarted.</P></TD></TR></TBODY></TABLE></DIV>
<DIV class=FixletProperty>
<H4>File Size:</H4>801.35 MB</DIV>
<DIV class=FixletProperty>
<H4>CVE:</H4>CVE-2014-6277, CVE-2014-7186, CVE-2014-7187, CVE-2014-8836, CVE-2014-8837, CVE-2014-4460, CVE-2014-4481, CVE-2014-4498, CVE-2014-4499, CVE-2014-1595, CVE-2014-8817, CVE-2014-4484, CVE-2014-4483, CVE-2014-4485, CVE-2014-8819, CVE-2014-8820, CVE-2014-8821, CVE-2014-4486, CVE-2014-4487, CVE-2014-4488, CVE-2014-4489, CVE-2014-8822, CVE-2014-8830, CVE-2014-8838, CVE-2014-8835, CVE-2014-4495, CVE-2014-8824, CVE-2014-4491, CVE-2014-4461, CVE-2014-8826, CVE-2014-4492, CVE-2014-8827, CVE-2014-8517, CVE-2014-3566, CVE-2014-3567, CVE-2014-3568, CVE-2014-8832, CVE-2014-4389, CVE-2014-8823, CVE-2014-8825, CVE-2014-4371, CVE-2014-4419, CVE-2014-4420, CVE-2014-4421, CVE-2014-8839, CVE-2014-8833, CVE-2014-8834</DIV>]]></Description>
    <Relevance>(exists string &quot;ProductVersion&quot; whose (it as string = &quot;10.10&quot;) of dictionary of it) of file &quot;/System/Library/CoreServices/SystemVersion.plist&quot;</Relevance>
